Subject: [PATCH] Put the hardware cache limit in configs_device

The product SimpleDeviceConfig RRO replaces configs_base as a whole. The
common vendor configs_base item is therefore invisible on the installed
product, leaving ActivityManager at its 1024-process platform default.
Keep the existing intended value of 32 in configs_device, which the boot
receiver applies after configs_base. Leave the compaction setting untouched.

--- a/overlay/packages/apps/SimpleDeviceConfig/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/packages/apps/SimpleDeviceConfig/res/values/config.xml
@@ -16,7 +16,11 @@
         <!-- ART heap compaction for cached apps -->
         <item>activity_manager/use_compaction=true</item>
 
-        <!-- Allow more cached apps in the background -->
+    </string-array>
+
+    <!-- configs_base belongs to the platform/product overlay. Keep hardware
+         defaults in configs_device so that the product array cannot hide them. -->
+    <string-array name="configs_device">
         <item>activity_manager/max_cached_processes=32</item>
     </string-array>
 </resources>
